# Line endings are decided here, not by each contributor's git config.
#
# Without this file the committed bytes depend on `core.autocrlf`, which the Git for Windows
# installer defaults to `true`. A contributor with that default would commit CRLF into the shell
# scripts and `android/gradlew`, and they would then die on Linux with:
#
#     bash: line 1: $'\r': command not found
#
# `.editorconfig` cannot prevent this: it is an editor convention and has no effect on what git
# writes into the object database.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only entry points genuinely want CRLF.
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf
*.ps1   text eol=crlf

# Never normalise binaries.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.ico   binary
*.icns  binary
*.jar   binary
*.apk   binary
*.aab   binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks   binary

# Generated / vendored: collapsed by default in review and excluded from language statistics.
# Deliberately NOT `-diff`: a dependency bump is exactly the change a reviewer must be able to read,
# and `linguist-generated` already hides the noise unless someone asks to see it.
tauri/package-lock.json      linguist-generated
tauri/src-tauri/Cargo.lock   linguist-generated
tauri/src-tauri/rnnoise/**   linguist-vendored
